// A discarded statement-position literal whose record holds a list of an un-annotated function.
//
// Nothing consumes the value, so no row is ever minted for the record; building it has no
// effect, so it must emit nothing rather than refuse. The literal rides SETUP, which places it
// in the delivery's own scope, so every scope position grades the discarded statement; the
// delivered value is a plain constant that proves the program ran past it.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function inc0(a) { return a + 1 }
// @@SETUP@@
[{ fs: [inc0] }]
// @@VALUE@@
7
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
7
